WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:02.850
Mind Your Decisions, I'm Presh Talwalkar.

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:09.000
One chicken has the same weight as one cat + one owl.(c = a + o)

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:13.139
2 chickens have the same weight as 3 turtles.(2c = 3t)

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:19.770
Finally, one owl and one turtle together have the same weight as one cat.(o + t = c)

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:22.560
The question is:

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:26.400
how many owls will balance exactly one cat?

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:32.279
This problem is adapted from a tweet from Manshead's Maths Department.

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:39.689
Pause the video if you'd like to give it a try ,and when you're ready, keep watching to learn how to solve this problem.

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:59.289
You could solve this problem using algebra, but I will present a visual approach to this logic puzzle.

00:01:00.230 --> 00:01:05.319
The weight of one chicken is equal to that of one cat plus one owl,

00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:09.609
so two chickens will have the weight of two cats and two owls.

00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:15.249
Now we will add the weight of three owls to both sides of the balance.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:20.109
Since we're adding the same way to both sides, it doesn't affect the balance.

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:26.739
We also know that one owl plus one turtle has the same weight as one cat.

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:30.430
We'll make this substitution on the right hand side.

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:39.549
We can now remove equal weight from both sides of the weighing scale. We'll remove the weight of two cats:

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:46.179
we are left with one cat and five owls, and this will be our answer.

00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:54.550
It takes exactly five owls to balance one cat, and we've solved this puzzle using just logic.

00:01:55.880 --> 00:02:00.130
Thanks for making Mind Your Decisions one of the best channels on YouTube, and as

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:04.509
always, thanks for watching, and thanks for your support.

